10
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:36,000
Master and Commander: The Far Side of the World is a 2003 American epic period war-drama film
co-written, produced and directed by Peter Weir, set during the Napoleonic Wars.

11
01:03:15,000 --> 01:03:21,000
The film's plot and characters are loosely adapted from novels in author Patrick O'Brian's
Aubrey–Maturin series, which includes 20 completed novels of Jack Aubrey's naval career.

12
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
The film stars Russell Crowe as Aubrey, captain in the
Royal Navy, and Paul Bettany as Dr.

13
01:14:45,000 --> 01:14:51,000
Stephen Maturin, the ship's surgeon.

14
01:20:30,000 --> 01:20:36,000
This was the second onscreen collaboration for Crowe and Bettany,
who previously co-starred in 2001's A Beautiful Mind.

15
01:26:15,000 --> 01:26:21,000
The film was a personal project of 20th Century Fox executive
Tom Rothman, who recruited Weir to direct.

16
01:32:00,000 --> 01:32:06,000
Filming took place on the open sea, on replica ships in the water
tanks of Baja Studios, and in the Galápagos Islands.

17
01:37:45,000 --> 01:37:51,000
The film, which cost US$150 million to make, was a co-production of 20th Century Fox, Miramax
Films, Universal Pictures, and Samuel Goldwyn Films, and released on November 14, 2003.

18
01:43:30,000 --> 01:43:36,000
The film received critical acclaim and grossed $212 million worldwide.

19
01:49:15,000 --> 01:49:21,000
It garnered Weir the BAFTA Award for Best Direction.

20
01:55:00,000 --> 01:55:06,000
At the 76th Academy Awards, the film was nominated in ten
categories, including Best Picture and Best Director.

21
02:00:45,000 --> 02:00:51,000
It won Best Cinematography and Best Sound Editing.

22
02:06:30,000 --> 02:06:36,000
The film explores themes of ship, navy, based on
novel or book, surgeon, royal navy.

23
02:12:15,000 --> 02:12:21,000
The tone is dark and emotional.
